---
// VI4 — preview-only typography route (AGENTS.md §12.3).
//
// Renders a real case study in the current treatment and in the two candidate
// body faces: the neutral system sans the owner already approved, and the
// self-hosted IBM Plex Sans candidate (`--font-sans`). It is not linked from
// the navigation or the homepage, and it changes nothing on the real pages.
// Astro's sitemap integration has no filter configured here, so this route
// does appear in sitemap-0.xml — reported, not silently fixed.
//
// The single property under test is the BODY text face. Headings stay
// Source Serif 4 (`--font-display`), code and metadata stay IBM Plex Mono
// (`--font-mono`). Only the preview route references the new `--font-sans`
// token; the real pages are untouched.
import { getEntry, render } from "astro:content";
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";

const entry = await getEntry(
	"docs",
	"case-studies/htb/machines/linux/helix",
);
if (!entry) {
	throw new Error(
		"preview/typography: case study 'helix' not found in the docs collection.",
	);
}
const { Content } = await render(entry);
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: "Preview — sans body, serif headings (VI4)",
		description:
			"Preview-only route for judging one typography change: Source Serif 4 headings with a sans body. Shows the current serif body alongside the approved system sans and the self-hosted IBM Plex Sans candidate on the real Helix case study.",
	}}
>
	<p class="vi4-banner" role="note">
		<strong>Preview route — not part of the published site.</strong> It
		tests one property only: the body text face.
	</p>

	<h2>What this preview is for</h2>
	<p>
		The site currently sets body copy in Source Serif 4, with IBM Plex Mono
		for metadata. This route shows the same case study with the body copy in
		the two candidate sans faces, to make the final pick before anything
		real is changed.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Under test:</strong> the body face only — serif headings
			with a sans body.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Unchanged:</strong> headings (Source Serif 4), code and
			metadata (IBM Plex Mono), palette, spacing, layout and font sizes.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Trade-off:</strong> the system stack adds <i>no</i> asset
			and renders natively, but looks different on Windows, macOS and
			Linux, so the site's typographic identity becomes machine-dependent.
			IBM Plex Sans costs two small woff2 files but keeps the deliberate
			self-hosted identity consistent, and pairs with the Plex Mono
			already in use.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Three candidates for the body face</h2>
	<p>
		The same representative passage from the Helix case study, in the
		current treatment and in the two candidate sans faces.
	</p>
	<div class="vi4-compare">
		<section class="vi4-panel vi4-serif" aria-labelledby="vi4-current">
			<h3 id="vi4-current">Current — Source Serif 4 body</h3>
			<p>
				Helix is a Medium-rated Hack The Box Linux lab in which an
				unauthenticated Apache NiFi instance on a virtual host is abused
				through CVE-2023-34468 — an H2-backed <code>DBCPConnectionPool</code>
				driving an <code>ExecuteSQL</code> processor — to gain command
				execution as the NiFi service account.
			</p>
			<pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;TARGET_IP&gt; --ulimit 5000 -- -Pn -sC -sV -oN &lt;OUT_FILE&gt;</code></pre>
		</section>
		<section class="vi4-panel vi4-system" aria-labelledby="vi4-system">
			<h3 id="vi4-system">System sans — approved direction</h3>
			<p>
				Helix is a Medium-rated Hack The Box Linux lab in which an
				unauthenticated Apache NiFi instance on a virtual host is abused
				through CVE-2023-34468 — an H2-backed <code>DBCPConnectionPool</code>
				driving an <code>ExecuteSQL</code> processor — to gain command
				execution as the NiFi service account.
			</p>
			<pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;TARGET_IP&gt; --ulimit 5000 -- -Pn -sC -sV -oN &lt;OUT_FILE&gt;</code></pre>
		</section>
		<section class="vi4-panel vi4-plex" aria-labelledby="vi4-plex">
			<h3 id="vi4-plex">IBM Plex Sans — self-hosted candidate</h3>
			<p>
				Helix is a Medium-rated Hack The Box Linux lab in which an
				unauthenticated Apache NiFi instance on a virtual host is abused
				through CVE-2023-34468 — an H2-backed <code>DBCPConnectionPool</code>
				driving an <code>ExecuteSQL</code> processor — to gain command
				execution as the NiFi service account.
			</p>
			<pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;TARGET_IP&gt; --ulimit 5000 -- -Pn -sC -sV -oN &lt;OUT_FILE&gt;</code></pre>
		</section>
	</div>

	<h2>Full case study in the proposed treatment</h2>
	<p>
		The real <i>Helix</i> case study, rendered in the self-hosted
		<i>IBM Plex Sans</i> candidate: dense prose, a command block, tables and
		the full heading hierarchy.
	</p>
	<div class="vi4-plex vi4-full">
		<Content />
	</div>
</StarlightPage>

<style is:global>
	/* Candidate body faces. Headings and code keep their existing explicit
	   faces from portfolio.css, so only inherited body copy changes. */
	.vi4-system {
		font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica,
			Arial, sans-serif;
	}
	.vi4-plex {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
	}
	.vi4-serif {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
	}
	.vi4-banner {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-accent);
		border-radius: var(--portfolio-radius);
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		background: var(--portfolio-accent-soft);
		color: var(--portfolio-accent-strong);
	}
	.vi4-compare {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.vi4-panel {
		border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
		border-radius: var(--portfolio-radius);
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--portfolio-surface-raised);
	}
	.vi4-panel h3 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.vi4-panel pre {
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	.vi4-full {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
		margin-top: 2rem;
		padding-top: 1rem;
	}
	@media (max-width: 48rem) {
		.vi4-compare {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
